abstract: >-
  Agentpower (AP) is a unit of cognitive work output measuring the total
  annual output of one knowledge worker. One AP equals the cognitive output
  of one full-time knowledge worker, unaided by AI, over one year. The AP
  Ratio (Total Cognitive Output / Human Headcount) provides a universal
  metric for AI-augmented productivity across professions and sectors.
  Introduced in the essay "Horsepower Then, Agentpower Now" (Pale Blue Dot,
  April 2026).
